{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 33, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a 2010 biographical drama film directed by david fincher and written by ben jessin and aaron sorkin. the film is based on the true story of the founding of mark zuckerberg's social networking site facebook.\n\nthe film takes place in 2003 and follows the story of mark zuckerberg (played by jesse eisenberg), a college student at harvard university, who creates a website calledfacebook.com. zuckerberg's goal is to create a social networking site that allows users to create profiles, connect with friends, and share information.\n\nas facebook gains popularity, zuckerberg's relationship with his college roommates and fellow developers, eduardo saverin (andoni gerson), and chad hurley (mason lee), becomes increasingly complicated. zuckerberg's obsessive focus on facebook leads to conflicts with his friends and colleagues, and he begins to neglect his relationships and his studies.\n\nmeanwhile, rebecca kirkpatrick (dakota fanning), a graduate student, starts a class-action lawsuit against facebook, claiming that the site's terms of service infringe on users' rights to intellectual property. zuckerberg's lawyers, led by jeremy ho (jesse plemons), work to defend facebook against the lawsuit.\n\nalongside the drama and conflict, the film also explores themes of identity, class, and the consequences of success. zuckerberg's character is portrayed as a complex and multifaceted individual, driven by a desire to create something new and innovative, but also struggling with the pressures of fame and the weight of responsibility.\n\nthe film features strong performances from the cast, particularly jesse eisenberg, who brings a nuanced and introspective portrayal of zuckerberg to life. the cinematography and editing are also noteworthy, capturing the frenetic energy of the college campus and the frenzied pace of the facebook's rapid growth.\n\none of the standout aspects of the film is its attention to detail. the film's script is meticulously researched, and the production design is spot-on, capturing the look and feel of harvard university and the facebook offices.\n\nthe film received widespread critical acclaim, with many praising its direction, writing, and performances. david fincher's direction is masterful, balancing the drama and tension with a sense of realism and authenticity. aaron sorkin's script is witty and insightful, capturing the complexities of the facebook phenomenon.\n\noverall, the social network is a gripping and thought-provoking film that offers a fascinating look at the early days of facebook and the complex personalities involved. it is a must-see for anyone interested in technology, social media, or the impact of the internet on society.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.20552276074886322}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.00030310326837934554}, {"token": " network", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.04680052399635315}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.0009606037638150156}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.5348334312438965}, {"token": "201", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": "0", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " bi", "logprob": -2.785822629928589}, {"token": "ographical", "logprob": -9.179073458653875e-06}, {"token": " drama", "logprob": -0.002906386274844408}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.001629216712899506}, {"token": " directed", "logprob": -0.15210804343223572}, {"token": " by", "logprob": -0.00031609306461177766}, {"token": " david", "logprob": -0.03087707795202732}, {"token": " fin", "logprob": -1.5258672647178173e-05}, {"token": "cher", "logprob": -0.39821040630340576}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -1.0174468755722046}, {"token": " written", "logprob": -0.00029666791670024395}, {"token": " by", "logprob": -2.3841830625315197e-06}, {"token": " ben", "logprob": -2.0583505630493164}, {"token": " j", "l